course: dictionary
lesson: 11526
title: The allocator, who shares things out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An allocator is a person or thing that shares out or gives out parts of something, such as money, places or jobs. Think of it as the one who divides things up.
explain: «The teacher was the seat allocator for the school trip.» She decided who sat where, so she shared out the seats. The clue is the word shares: an allocator gives each person a part.
explain: In computing, a memory allocator is a part of a computer program. It hands out memory space when the program needs it. In maths, an allocator may share an amount into parts. In every case, ask yourself: who is giving things out here?
fact: An allocator is a person or thing that shares out or gives out parts of something.
fact: «Seat allocator» means the person who decides where people sit.
fact: In computing, a memory allocator hands out memory space when it is needed.
fact: «Allocator» is a formal, technical word, so you will meet it in computing and maths.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in the words "the one who shares out". If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
exercise: «The seat allocator put Mia by the window.» Who is the seat allocator? | *The person who decided where Mia sat | The bus driver | The child sitting next to Mia | The person who painted the classroom
exercise: In computing, what does a memory allocator do? | Deletes all the files on a computer | Makes the screen brighter | *Hands out memory space when a program needs it | Plays music while you work
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a person or thing that shares things out: «The allocator shared the cakes between the three friends.» | cakes | three | *allocator | friends
test: «The allocator shared the jobs fairly among the team.» What is the allocator doing? | Shouting the team's names | *Sharing out the jobs | Cooking the dinner | Cleaning the windows
test: In maths, an allocator might share an amount into parts. Which example fits? | Walking to school in the rain | Reading a book about dragons | Painting a picture of a tree | *Splitting 12 sweets equally between 3 children
exam: «The school's seat allocator gave the front row to the youngest pupils.» Who or what is the allocator? | The front row itself | The youngest pupil in the front row | *The person who decided where the pupils sat | The school bell
